    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Real or Not?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Here are some equations:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Real or Not?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Which equations will have real solutions, and which ones will not? Write your prediction in the table. Pause here for discussion.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Real or Not?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What advice would you give to someone who is trying to figure out whether a quadratic equation has real solutions?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Create three different quadratic equations. At least one should have solutions with an imaginary part, and at least one should have solutions with only real parts.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Solve your equations. Write down your equations and their solutions in the table.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "By looking at the graph of a quadratic function, we can tell whether it has real zeros or not. The real zeros are the \\(x\\)-coordinates of the points where the graph touches the \\(x\\)-axis. So, if the graph doesn't touch the \\(x\\)-axis at…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can also tell whether \\(y=ax^2+bx+c\\) has real zeros by using the quadratic formula strategically, since the quadratic formula tells us the \\(x\\)-values that make a quadratic function be 0. For reference, here is the quadratic formula:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle x=\\dfrac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Imaginary numbers are the square roots of negative numbers, so it will be helpful to look at the part of the quadratic formula that involves a square root, which is \\(\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}\\). If \\(4ac\\) is greater than \\(b^2\\), then the number…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, consider the quadratic function \\(y=x^2+2x+2\\). How can we tell if it has real zeros?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "One way is to look at the graph, shown here. Since its graph doesn't intersect the \\(x\\)-axis, this function doesn't have any real zeros.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L19-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "19.3: Make Your Own",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can also tell by checking whether \\(4ac\\) is greater than \\(b^2\\). Since \\(a=1\\), \\(b=2\\), and \\(c=2\\), \\(b^2-4ac=\\text-4\\), so the zeros of this function have an imaginary part. We can find out exactly what the zeros are by using the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
